  "step_semantics": {
    "adam_step_note": "Adam state['step'] equals the training iteration MINUS one lost increment per densification event (events at 500..14900 every 100 iterations replace the parameter objects; their .grad is None at the event iteration so torch Adam skips the increment). At 15000 the step is 14856 for every parameter and increments on every post-densification step. The probe's update_learning_rate(C+1) + optimizer.step() therefore reproduces training iteration C+1 EXACTLY (same step counter, same bias correction). This is the frozen baseline's own semantics, not a defect: adam_step_values are equal across all 5 parameter groups at every checkpoint."
